": 23, "text": "GPT-6.1 Sol's G6 was the worst move of its game, costing 27.0 points and dropping the lead from -0.4 to -27.5. The engine's choice was E8."}, {"turn": 24, "text": "The 20k's F8 answered with the worst move of its own game, losing 23.3 points. It brought Black's lead from -27.5 back to -4.2, so the game was still alive."}, {"turn": 36, "text": "The 20k's F9 lost 10.0 points, taking Black from +8.1 down to... in fact it moved the lead from -2.0 to +8.1 in Black's favour, so Black's lead grew to +8.1. Black's J7 then lost 8.1, and the lead fell to +0.0. The swings on the top-right edge were large on both sides."}, {"turn": 59, "text": "GPT-6.1 Sol's B5 lost 0.0 points. From here the position settled at about +2.3, and the remaining moves each lost under half a point except the 20k's B8, which lost 3.9 and lifted Black to +7.7 for the final +8.0."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every command either called mcp__go__play with a move the player had already chosen, or ran the `inspect` flood-fill (groups/liberties from the returned board), the final area count in step 46, or record-keeping (store/load, SGF, game-017 files, AGENTS.md patches). None of it loops over candidate moves, scores or ranks moves, or plays sequences forward.", "stop": false}}